# Source-controlled voxel-building blueprints live here. Filename stem = blueprint id
# (BuildingBlueprintCatalog.load_path overwrites whatever the JSON claims).
#
# EMPTY SINCE 2026-07-24 (commit aabdf198), and it cannot be refilled yet.
# That commit wiped BrickCatalog.BRICKS to {} and retired the building brick
# editor scene, taking harbouroffice.json and warehouse.json with it. Every write
# path gates on BrickCatalog.has(): BuildingLayout.set_brick / place_footprint
# return false, and BuildingRules.validate reports "Unknown brick", so load_path
# push_errors and returns null. The only JSON that would load today is one with
# zero cells — a placeholder that asserts nothing.
#
# Do not invent placeholder buildings by hand. The blocker is the vocabulary, not
# the directory: the first real blueprint can only be authored once BRICKS has
# definitions again. Structure Studio does not fill this directory — it authors
# structure_plan_v1 into resources/data/structures/.
#
# tests/building_blueprint_test.gd covers the brick-independent half of the
# pipeline and trips when either the vocabulary or the first blueprint returns.
